---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import AuthorBio from '../components/AuthorBio.astro';
import { rankedDirectory } from '../lib/ranking';
import { PRIMARY_SOURCES } from '../data/sources';

const ranked = rankedDirectory();
const scored = ranked;
---

<Layout
  title="Methodology — SuretyResearch"
  description="Every name in the register is sorted by the public-signal score printed on its card, including the Cornerstone Network Preferred Partner."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">House rules</p>
      <h1>How the register is ranked.</h1>
      <p>
        Every name is sorted by a score built only from the public signals printed on its card. Integrity First Insurance, the Cornerstone Network Preferred Partner, is scored on the same rule.
      </p>
      <AuthorBio />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>1. The Cornerstone network partner is labeled, not pinned</h2>
      <p>
        Integrity First Insurance is the Cornerstone Network Preferred Partner, the desk this register uses for licensing and surety placement inside the Cornerstone network. Its card prints that label so the relationship is plain.
      </p>
      <p>
        Its position comes from the same public-signal score as every other name. Travelers’ public agent directory lists surety among the lines at the agency’s published address. Bond work is coordinated with Covered by Cornerstone and Cornerstone Surety Bonds.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Every name is scored, then sorted</h2>
      <p>
        The order is the public-signal score. A missing signal adds zero points.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>BBB letter grade: A+ 22, A 18, A− 14, B-band 8 (grade only).</li>
        <li>AM Best, when a company page or AM Best source is cited: A++ 20, A+ 16, A 13, A− 10.</li>
        <li>Years since founding (capped): 0.35 points per year, max 24.</li>
        <li>Nationwide placement listed: 18. Otherwise 2 points per known state, max 18.</li>
        <li>Bond-category breadth: 4 points per series (license, contract, commercial, court).</li>
        <li>Treasury Circular 570 mention cited on the card: 8.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Ties break by older founding year, then A–Z. The score is printed on each file.</p>

      <h2>3. Current order</h2>
      <p>
        The table is the live order for this build: {scored.length} scored names.
      </p>
      <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>#</th><th>Name</th><th>Score</th><th>Kind</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {ranked.map((a) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{String(a.rank).padStart(2, '0')}</td>
              <td><a href={`/agencies/${a.slug}/`}>{a.name}</a></td>
              <td>{a.score}</td>
              <td>{a.kind}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      </div>

      <h2>4. Where the outside figures come from</h2>
      <p>
        Carrier limits and statutory thresholds on the guides come from the primary sources below. The score above is this register’s own arithmetic on the signals each card cites.
      </p>
      <ul class="source-list">
        {PRIMARY_SOURCES.map((source) => (
          <li><a href={source.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{source.label}</a></li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <p>
        Federal construction contracts of more than $100,000 for a public building or public work require a performance bond and a payment bond under <a href="https://uscode.house.gov/view.xhtml?req=granuleid:USC-prelim-title40-section3131&num=0&edition=prelim">40 U.S.C. § 3131</a>. A property broker must have a $75,000 surety bond or trust fund under <a href="https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-49/subtitle-B/chapter-III/subchapter-B/part-387/subpart-C/section-387.307">49 CFR § 387.307</a>. Circular 570, effective August 1, 2026, lists the per-bond underwriting limitation for each certified company.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Signal date</h2>
      <p>
        Signal dates on the cards are stamped August 23, 2026. Open the source URL on the card for the record that was cited.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
